# Trivy ignore list for the image scan (CI: input `trivyignores`, threshold HIGH,CRITICAL). Every entry has a reason and an expiry date
# (APPLICATION-STANDARDS section 5.1); after the date Trivy reports it again.
#
# Base image python:3.12-slim = Debian 13.7. On 2026-11-14 Trivy 0.76.0 reported these HIGH findings in OS packages. For all but the two zlib
# entries Debian has no fixed version yet (status "affected" / "fix_deferred"); for zlib the fix (deb13u1) is not yet in the base image.
# Not reachable: the load generator is a batch process that only makes outgoing HTTP requests (no listener, no archive, sqlite, mount or
# user-management use), runs as UID 10001 and has no shell access path from the network.
# Review when the base image is rebuilt; remove entries that Trivy no longer reports.
